[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Breakfast or Lunch?]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:10.47]Why was the writer's aunt surprised? | 作者的姑妈为什么感到惊讶？
[00:16.00]It was Sunday. | 那是个星期天。
[00:17.99]I never get up early on Sundays. | 星期天我从来不早起。
[00:22.03]I sometimes stay in bed until lunchtime. | 有时我要一直躺到吃午饭的时候。
[00:26.81]Last Sunday I got up very late. | 上个星期天我起得很晚。
[00:31.06]I looked out of the window. | 我望望窗外。
[00:33.45]It was dark outside. | 外面一片昏暗。
[00:35.84]'What a day!' I thought. | “鬼天气！”我想。
[00:39.60]'It's raining again.' | “又下雨了。”
[00:42.61]Just then, the telephone rang. | 正在这时，电话铃响了。
[00:46.04]It was my aunt Lucy. | 是我姑妈露西打来的。
[00:49.04]'I've just arrived by train,' she said. | “我刚下火车，”她说。
[00:53.09]'I'm coming to see you.' | “我这就来看你。”
[00:56.01]'But I'm still having breakfast,' I said. | “可我还在吃早饭，”我说。
[01:00.54]'What are you doing?' she asked. | “你在干什么？”她问道。
[01:03.84]'I'm having breakfast,' I repeated. | “我在吃早饭，”我又说了一遍。
[01:07.50]'Dear me,' she said. | “天哪，”她说。
[01:10.40]'Do you always get up so late? | “你总是起得这么晚吗？
[01:13.39]It's one o'clock!' | 已经一点钟了！”
